{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291639,"nonce":"OFOPwgUa/UVLt+3IFJ3JkwJ9X5w=","title":"zyntax_wasm: call_indirect_by_handle reports interpreter errors as Pending","message":"crates/zyntax_wasm/src/lib.rs call_indirect_by_handle returns 0 for an unknown closure handle, a null ACTIVE_RUNTIME, a non-Int result and an Err from call_function. A poll fn returning 0 means Pending, so run_async_impl's first poll and the resume path treat an interpreter error as a parked task. The JS Promise then never settles and nothing is logged.\n\nThis hid 5a54699 (AsyncSaveSlot of an undefined value) for months: the only symptom was a test's own 5 s timeout.\n\nWanted: an error from the poll fn fails the task. For example, run_async_impl returns a runtime_err RunResult on the first poll, and the resume path calls js_complete_task with ok=0 and logs the message, so the host sees what is missing.","files":null}]}